" seemingly being the main challengers. But Sieben surprised in qualifying with 1:59.63 to move on to the final."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final started as expected as Groß went out fast, trailed early by Vidal. Morales made his move at 100 metres. Sieben was out in lane six, unwatched by the crowd and the other swimmers, but by the final turn he had moved to Vidal’s shoulder, who was in lane five. In the last 25 metres it was very close, with all four swimmers coming to the wall almost together and no one was certain who had won. In one of the biggest upsets in Olympic swimming history, it was Jon Sieben, who said later, “I only knew I’d won when I turned around and saw on the board.” Sieben finished in a world record 1:57.04, 1/100th of a second ahead of Groß’s mark, with Groß in second, Vidal and third, and Morales pushed off the podium despite swimming 1:57.75."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "30"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/45287"} "Jon Sieben"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "1:59.63 (2 h4)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:57.04 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "196"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47812"} "Michael Groß"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRG.png"}] "FRG"]] [:td {} "1:58.72 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:57.40 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"}